      "proposition": {
        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>While many young people have found jobs and built careers, some have struggled to complete their courses</p><p></p><p>The crisis in the youth employment market, with <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/aug/27/neets-figures-youth-unemployment-april-june\">almost a million young people not in education, employment or training (Neet)</a> across the UK, has placed fresh emphasis on ways of getting employees into the workforce.</p><p>The government hopes to increase focus on technical and vocational learning in England from the age of 14. In parallel, there is an ambition to create thousands more apprenticeships.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/education/2026/sep/01/apprenticeships-apprentices-young-people-vocational-training\">Continue reading...</a>"
